Sophie Casterwill used Feyone as her last [[Titans|Titan]] against a number of Suits at [[Sutos Island]]. She was able to send one of them to the ground before going back to her amulet after two Suits fired a [[Raypulse]] spell at her. {{Source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

In an all out attack against a couple of [[The Organization|Organization]] Suits that ambushed the Huntik team at [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]], Sophie invoked Feyone alongside [[Icarus]]. Feyone was able to take out an [[Enforcer]] Titan with the assist of Icarus. {{Source|Home Turf}}

Feyone was invoked by Sophie alongside Icarus and [[Sabriel]] to fight [[Zhalia Moon]] and her [[Kilthane]] inside the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. {{Source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

Deep in the Turkish forest, Sophie showcased Feyone and Sabriel to the [[Amazons]] upon them asking where her [[Titans]] were, surprised Sophie was a Seeker. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}}

Inside [[King Solomon's Mines]], in the battle for the [[Tao|Legendary Titan of Spirit]], Feyone and Sabriel were used by Sophie to battle against [[Simon Judeau|the Professor]] and his [[Suits]] alongside several other Titans invoked by the [[Huntik Foundation|Huntik]] team. Feyone was sent back to her amulet after being hit by an [[Enforcer]]'s laser attack. {{Source|To Be Together}}

Sophie's Feyone was used in the final battle against the Professor inside his [[The Professor's castle|castle]] in response to a Suit's [[Terrapede]] Titan. Feyone quickly got grabbed by Terrapede, being sent to her amulet after being hit by its blast attack. {{Source|The Divine Comedy}} When faced against the Professor in his invocation chamber, Sophie again invoked Feyone alongside [[Hoplite]]. Feyone managed to strike [[Behemoth]] and later on, [[Tao]], helping stall the Professor's ritual to invoke [[Overlos]]. {{Source|The Mission}}

Feyone was used by Sophie inside a hidden observatory at the [[Tower of Nostradamus]] to fight with [[the Organization]] for the [[Nostradamus' Scrying Glass|Scrying Glass]]. Feyone blasted a Suit and the container that held the Glass off Hoffman's hands, before being later taken out by his [[Rippleburst]] spell. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

Inside the [[Cave of the Casterwills]], on a test to retrieve [[Sorcerel]]'s amulet, Sophie pondered invoking Feyone and Icarus to take out [[Coralgolem]] and [[Undine]]. However, she gave up on the idea upon realizing that the test wasn't meant to test her fighting abilities. {{Source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

Due to Feyone's notable agility, she was invoked once again by Sophie Casterwill to fight [[Rassimov]]'s [[Legion]] by the [[Spiral Mark]]. Legion managed to grab her, partially assimilating Feyone and damaging her amulet. Upon Lok Lambert destroying Legion's amulet, all of the damage was reversed. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}}

