=== White's Feyone ===
Feyone, alongside [[Mallory]]'s Icarus,  was invoked by [[White]] to help them strike the Huntik team from above while they were reaching the coastline leading to the [[Cave of the Casterwills]]. She managed to hit Sophie Casterwill, who was trying to reach the two Titans with [[Hyperstride]], sending her back to the water. [[Dante Vale|Dante]]'s [[Metagolem]] threw Feyone off the edge of the elevated position by throwing boulders at her, and she was finished off by Zhalia's [[Kilthane]]. 

=== Lucas' Feyone ===
Lucas used his Feyone Titan to fight the Huntik team at the [[Casterwill Library]]. Feyone aimed her energy beam at Dante Vale, but he was able to dodge it. She was then sent back to her amulet in a quick sequence of attacks by Sophie Casterwill's [[Sorcerel|Sorecerel]]. {{Source|Chasing Void}}

=== Focauld Casterwill's and Rue Guardians' Feyone Titans ===
After a long spell, the Rue Guardians, with [[Focauld Casterwill|Focauld Casterwil]]<nowiki/>l's help, were able to invoke several Feyone and Icarus Titans, along with a Coralgolem Titan, housed inside the [[Fortress of Iron Will]] to protect it from the huge [[Blood Spiral]] army trying to invade it. Upon seeing the many Titans, the Blood Spirals retreated from the battle. {{Source|The Spiral War}}

=== Feyone Titans of unspecified Seekers ===
One or more Feyone Titans were once assimilated by [[Legion]] in the past, which made use of Feyone's attacks against the Huntik team when they were trying to ambush [[Rassimov]]. With Feyone's energy blast attack, Legion knocked Den Fears and, later on, Sophie Casterwill to the ground, surpassing her [[Honorguard]] spell. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}

At a given time, an unspecified Feyone fought against [[DeFoe]] and one his Redcap Titans. {{Source|TCG:SAS-124|SAS-124}} Other unspecified Feyone Titans have also been seen. {{Source|SAS-055}}{{Source|SAS-119}}

== Abilities ==
Feyone is equipped with the unusual combination of light armor and heavy weaponry. With little more than a helmet and leather protecting her from attacks, one would think this female brawler Titan was doomed to fall to a well-placed jab, but she leverages her lack of armor perfectly, moving with a speed and grace that no armor-clad Titan can match. Watching her dodge the strikes of her enemies is like watching a giant do gymnastics: it doesn't seem possible with her size, but Titans regularly surpass the expectations of humans. Feyone is also able to project an energy beam from her hands when outstretched. She carries herself with serenity both off and on the battlefield. She is also very skilled with her sword.

